 Tennecked one knit up his brows, and, wrought up with wrath, said to him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.929,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d92292afe54e926c21fbc872fa736e00c73b64d0ed47959b0ab88bdf00de4c1b","compact":"77265d1539aedbd50a3124d4dc0c6de8e295b3f8688e9f6f1dd817373be3f4fe","nasal":"5cf7c85f35934a77d7ee564875feb80fc9280d930f92e5accf3b35ecc09e6400"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":22,"english":"I am worthy of being honoured by you, like your superior. What needs this verbal travail? Do you what is fit.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.514,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5c7884be6e65c63dd4ee0ef303b27bcd9143459ffd1de5642653a0332010b4e5","compact":"3e25f6306962dad8d55c1ee9c2e8169d93e12399b8a3ee0b28a8599a9c394b1f","nasal":"3e25f6306962dad8d55c1ee9c2e8169d93e12399b8a3ee0b28a8599a9c394b1f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-23","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":23,"english":"Vain is the mention now of what I did either through stupor or delusion or pride of prowess. Now bethink you of what is proper.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.732,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051023","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"959044bb6d8eae5ac8925b4e974bf8f88a5aad851ebb10b91a06ff9968715346","compact":"13c26568316a6a777fcd7cafbf1737281e1efa8d7f2c325f01e149e5821baca8","nasal":"af0f65b330e59592879bf0d3e930c388de6e22c8f91f742bf277b3ecdd4c8d38"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-24","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":24,"english":"Do you through your prowess assuage the sorrow of mine springing from my impolitic conduct, if you cherish any feeling for me, if your strength stay and if you deem this business of mine as by far more momentous to you.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.644,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051024","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e38a3feab230bb8627d1641e18c6322222b3b340783aa5cb699a30416120ea30","compact":"ca02001786f3e7654dfe98b875716aaab34c8e85aecbec0371e9265b1c3df3c2","nasal":"92de0c915b3c0588561645ad5443531209b9de5d1f0aea9e623458fccdb42013"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-25","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":25,"english":"Do you through your prowess assuage the sorrow of mine springing from my impolitic conduct, if you cherish any feeling for me, if your strength stay and if you deem this business of mine as by far more momentous to you.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.438,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051025","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fae0f7b47e3c545f26fb5167876b845832ae112c837767e9177ef1fd0af7fc11","compact":"62d100794988034a0e381bc5e2d6e4cf284440c899edfb420e674ff5a8b08f98","nasal":"62d100794988034a0e381bc5e2d6e4cf284440c899edfb420e674ff5a8b08f98"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-26","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":26,"english":"He is a friend that succour one fallen in distress and is undergoing affliction; and he acts friendly that helped a person lapsing from the path of morality.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.689,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051026","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5324b5fce2db8c0ac957f42fefac6782af7dbd3f886e26e3a2953d660e38514a","compact":"0dd1845901fecb6a5030c943f63d2015d554c81c8d708d37347605677679ab9e","nasal":"9b9efa13c6ead46ed357c2dc55d62ebabe74bcca2ff819d3818397c864c9f1d3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-27","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":27,"english":"As he was speaking thus in words sedate yet severe, Kumbhakarma, concluding that Ravana was undelighted, makes his remarks mildly. And seeing his brother extremely sorry, Kumbhakarņa, pacifying him, gently said.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.847,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051027","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2424404db536a6bfb239889cc8c9b5626a1a53e4f4606a2346f0b03828aca1b4","compact":"6d16c2e25ae46a676b2141bd4d2fb285ce2462ff1b90e4cb32cce34f59ebabf9","nasal":"6d16c2e25ae46a676b2141bd4d2fb285ce2462ff1b90e4cb32cce34f59ebabf9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-28","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":28,"english":"As he was speaking thus in words sedate yet severe, Kumbhakarma, concluding that Ravana was undelighted, makes his remarks mildly. And seeing his brother extremely sorry, Kumbhakarņa, pacifying him, gently said.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051028","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3085dde678b8a25d52fabac3b9d7100435e49583e8b4fc1284fd69f0a9a5b492","compact":"c199663cd3bffa376b424fd7eceafd39411f4420ed7287357bdd9e308d3965b9","nasal":"d06ce24cd3c1788e87e97954bbb6515f9b9ebd3915aa1569f643b20452971dbf"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-29","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":29,"english":"O king, intently hear my words. O repressor of foes! O lord of Raksasas, banish this sorrow, and casting away your wrath, return you to nature.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051029","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1410c5e1d8d6d3cf9cc5bb38682f5bf4d964779c41bcf15ba3363623006a1b5e","compact":"75050526e29b374b0b592546387b4420d3c49a41d8e8d344e01458f30e732888","nasal":"9d5e2413f935009e206a278dd7cd7eab769fa0e329307b0f1189361d89a0bf7b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-30","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":30,"english":"O king, so long as I live, you must not suffer your heart to fare thus. Him will I slay for whom you grieve.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.845,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051030","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d57e80d76c79751f3041b46feb203aae408c7e7e98a9b1fa5c607b9b0933b5c5","compact":"b9f4a95cc0ab9a7cae7bd14cf1fa5b312ff126e50859ba5c8bbfc921e1543fb9","nasal":"b9f4a95cc0ab9a7cae7bd14cf1fa5b312ff126e50859ba5c8bbfc921e1543fb9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-31","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":31,"english":"But whatever condition you may be in, I must tell what is for your welfare; and therefore from sentiment of friendship as well as from fraternal affection I have spoken thus to you o King.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.672,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051031","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"399b4fcb6d2259caef51b1ed6c8cdeb016bf2745008f0354a97e0652efd36677","compact":"b9e38343c3cfb4c5d16b18f87cc8d38a517a2980be3b7da911f434e12c012b5b","nasal":"61db1ab3fd0e7c7b45335211464439bd0ff6cfeebaf7e5e084f9efbb29ef6b18"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-32","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":32,"english":"What a friend from affection should do at a time like this, I shall do the same. See the havoc I spread among the foes in fight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.682,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051032","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c537645e1300accb850b7b878ba28fec3bbd8af27f824b6e74643047757e5a0f","compact":"e680121ba171301a6ef7000683417ca105752fdcb1af354b9ba612f856d31862","nasal":"cfc05b1476eaca5cf4ce2bc4b1761ecb2072757add3ba367f1675d96ef5cc6bb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-33","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":33,"english":"O long-armed one, behold, on Rāma having been slain by me on the edge of battle along with his brother, the monkey-army in headlong flight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051033","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f6984f22acd934729f4214f3cb101710e056d5a6af3e00c3e835defa6988694d","compact":"6ea10124f361b3e9bad0b23845c59a015a29d98b57e8747da1306228f8c0790b","nasal":"f8c7915ddc6a22f749c680f0b242e0b44fbdd0819422b30fc7177058f5cf6ccc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-34","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":34,"english":"And today seeing Rāma's head brought by me from the field, be you, O long-armed one, happy; and let Sitā be overwhelmed with woe.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051034","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0feacc3450134378478cbf778418a7423b0254e459dcdb570c9a475b200e150c","compact":"76852292cd0d61832948c38189a7711b22f0ade11af97bce46588d42b764e5d5","nasal":"76852292cd0d61832948c38189a7711b22f0ade11af97bce46588d42b764e5d5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-35","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":35,"english":"And let those Raksasas in Lankā who have had their kindred slain (in battle), see that dear sight-Rāma slain (in fight).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051035","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6b63bf8c3fe51684098af6f9e3b090fd5bb0a057631a08595eb9342c4f241dfb","compact":"f9d32795c7864a6e3e38b0855373ebab70a7f73005968b85681042bcbca21086","nasal":"bebe21fd4ffc52d2b994c3c6fe5655df8d03da74f345b21fd22e6265c05fb21f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-36","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":36,"english":"Today shall I slaying the enemies in battle, wipe the tears of those who mourn their friend slain and are overwhelmed with grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.635,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051036","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e5f21ef89612ae78f71359017b9cd76c962ecfaad2ffe2bbb11a173ec929094c","compact":"d42e91de1cc77670cd9457350b974d0eafad8921c43d1447bf7ea4c23616753f","nasal":"b36af3d3c7cd2272e573731bb88cdd66025558fc8dd59b794e99bac0b2d27d85"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-37","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":37,"english":"To-day behold the lord of monkeys-Sugrivaresembling a mountain or a mass of clouds lighted up by (the living) sun, lying stretched on the field.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051037","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"11981850a34fee8f8f31be605b77b86aef8190b1a4f64a7fe5bd75ab5945c057","compact":"833d0cc56712573e1e36ac3235c490a4f579a63685551136a59542bdf206d9a2","nasal":"833d0cc56712573e1e36ac3235c490a4f579a63685551136a59542bdf206d9a2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-38","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":38,"english":"O repressor of foes, do you now command me O you of unparalleled prowess, you need not yourself face the foe in fight. I shall abolish your foes endowed with redoubted might. If even Śakra himself, and Yama, and the god of Fire, and the god of Wind, and Kubera, and Varuņa-shall range themselves against me, them shall I encounter in fight.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.328,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-37","DUTT-6-63-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051038","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7581bb657581636a045fb653c8f3eee5499361a7a30d03ea9ed2b55fad9d628e","compact":"5972d5a0722458489c0bd1514fa0d1b7b55f480cdd1ca7d0ce4e8e047b63a11d","nasal":"5972d5a0722458489c0bd1514fa0d1b7b55f480cdd1ca7d0ce4e8e047b63a11d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-39","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":39,"english":"I shall abolish your foes endowed with redoubted might. If even Śakra himself, and Yama, and the god of Fire, and the god of Wind, and Kubera, and Varuņa-shall range themselves against me, them shall I encounter in fight.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051039","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"908ae31445652226f083881ccab00d03f3b60728160bd896e85dc1d7bb1f4a49","compact":"f8a0b46007410a8f36c584f8977e81ac5c15463828b43a9fd0e7aee2ff2a4d0d","nasal":"f8a0b46007410a8f36c584f8977e81ac5c15463828b43a9fd0e7aee2ff2a4d0d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-40","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":40,"english":"Purandara himself is seized with fright at sight of me, having a body measuring a mountain, equipped with sharpened spears, furnished with sharp teeth, and setting up shouts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051040","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"84917f1c1ee8705d3c7f3bf0fe0caea3790ba9c5ff6aa12d3c7b969dda2fd31d","compact":"5cd6f950b84868bb6a20ee15591c2f5decc4d78e02a1a18fb4a0679e1a6a254a","nasal":"5cd6f950b84868bb6a20ee15591c2f5decc4d78e02a1a18fb4a0679e1a6a254a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-41","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":41,"english":"And who wishing to save himself shall be able to stay before me as I casting away my weapons keep pounding my enemies with celerity?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.486,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051041","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d06e66e126e4ac4e2874dc4cabeda882928aaa4923d3b5854ca2dcd2869e75f9","compact":"34ed3b7511aca546156af802d5fd905de1c9bd44263f63fb0ecc67961e92c254","nasal":"90f87ea9102b1fe392021f643d6aab1b20f395ad677228e4468ddbd0f171485a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-42","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":42,"english":"No need of the dart, or the mace, or the sword, or whetted arrows. I shall with my bare arms alone slay (Rāma) along with the thunderer himself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.46,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051042","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a1f70ce2849bd8a7e2c5feb31d96ed0b1cceb2d5f23ebc481c2ec60bace33c68","compact":"07a479fd70795ab4bfe15240bfbb0f191a4917e4c5dfd96e4920547720651366","nasal":"07a479fd70795ab4bfe15240bfbb0f191a4917e4c5dfd96e4920547720651366"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-43","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":43,"english":"If Raghava bear the impetus of my blows, the shall the vollies of my shafts drink his life blood.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.828,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-42"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051043","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e50d093dd663cd9e1f2de55772fa7f1c649a4228edc7c9a56a42bd539a870e38","compact":"85abec075093113e6c7f5d92018a63695fd18ae56d1a1eb1ec200722a2d0278e","nasal":"a1e1dcad23b4d646640e9f4dc9a3ab40615d93083941a018b2a70a9e50005e3c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-44","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":44,"english":"Why, O king, while I remain, did you burn in anxiety. And I am ready to sally out for compassing the destruction of your enemies.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-43"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051044","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"07e97e497f570c4df774da276e0b74be1cd4c0a44598161d0a937df0900a1f02","compact":"4cdcf68442cf65759cf55a71180f124401f87deadc8b837e64ecae2202d53b8b","nasal":"e239186399f1d953e9abee0088de20d0c1ca93d99de79386fbbff86b07a41ea4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-45","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":45,"english":"Cast off all terror of Rāma. I shall slay in battle Rāghava and Lakşmaņa and the exceedingly powerful Sugrīva and the Räksasadestroying Hanumān, who made Lankā blaze. I shall cat up the monkeys present in the encounter. And signal is the celebrity that I shall confer on you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.652,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-44"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051045","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"160b95a09906a6f84e8e33e382a4cd9245086aa584f51ccd3af89c8f9bfc1bc3","compact":"10f0f20578cc827a332d8a5bdd581ffb5fb665e7cc0ddccd68a5058be31c93c4","nasal":"62e52fb4ed7fee7f1f70bca4740c46a93ce66456e32b88b6fc00f93f2e26611f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-46","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":46,"english":"I go for securing felicity us huring in pleasures plenteous flowing from the destruction of Dasaratha's son. And slaying Rāma along with Lakşmaņa, I shall eat up all the foremost of monkey-bands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-48"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051046","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"352b41e54911f63b1995626799d705fa96eda981056da7d864d337812dfb7d9e","compact":"5b88649728cd5041eb53b83ac0fc66f1d780df9f815f7ec1a5d978dc3c8f2e56","nasal":"5b88649728cd5041eb53b83ac0fc66f1d780df9f815f7ec1a5d978dc3c8f2e56"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-51-47","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":51,"verse":47,"english":"Make merry, my king; today drink Varuni. Enjoy pleasures, banishing sorrow. And today on my having despatched Rāma to the mansion of Yama, Sītā shall come under your control for good.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.644,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-63-49"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6051047","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"047d43d46f731c68e76488f6d5446c3888e24473f432b0c339f8438c45285d0b","compact":"7afb94d919c3ca90083905d5d2b437e1a82ce9fc77a63830d77c8b013f124271","nasal":"7afb94d919c3ca90083905d5d2b437e1a82ce9fc77a63830d77c8b013f124271"}}]
